    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet on a gloriously private c. 0.75 acre, “Papion” is a versatile, bungalow style family home with development potential (subject to Planning Permission) in the south-west facing rear garden. Enjoying an exclusive location in The Burnaby, Erskine Avenue is one of the Burnaby's lesser travelled pretty pockets, ideally situated between Old Mill Road and Portland Road, offering the utmost of convenience being a short walk to the rugby and tennis clubs and an easy stroll home from Greystones Golf Club. \n\nThe owner occupiers have lovingly maintained this charming 4 bedroom, detached residence which has been their family home for over four decades during which time they have overseen a seamless extension, garage conversion and installation of a much loved gazebo in the serene rear garden. The impressive ground floor accommodation is approached through a pretty tiled entrance porch, opening from the entrance hallway to a welcoming sitting/dining room with a beautiful vista of the colour filled rear garden, while the wood burning stove caters for a cosy evenings in this open plan reception space. Access to the extended portion of the home is through double doors which lead one to the light-infused sunroom where French doors open to a smart paved patio at the back of the home. One will also find the well-appointed home office along with 2 exceptionally large double bedrooms which enjoy shared use of the “jack and jill” bathroom on this side of the property. The attic is floored for storage with a Stira staircase giving easy access to a large storage space which could be suitable for conversion, subject to Planning Permission.\n\nAlso radiating from the reception hall is a TV room or snug complete with wood burning stove which could be used as a playroom or a 5th bedroom. A single bedroom with built in wardrobe storage and full bathroom are to be found off the hallway heading towards the attractive kitchen/breakfast room with views of the south-west garden. From here one enters the area which has been cleverly converted from a former garage to a bright reading room and the practical utility room beyond which opens to the serene outdoors. Upstairs, the main bedroom suite boasts a beautiful dressing area with extensive built in wardrobes, ensuite shower room and further storage space in the eaves. \n\nThe expansive gardens of approx 0.75 acre are truly a delight, well screened from view and offering the keen gardener and nature lover plenty of interest in specimen trees and shrubs, an orchard section, kitchen garden, flowering bushes, all lending the gardens an array of year-round colour. In addition, the covered gazebo alongside Indian sandstone patio can be screened from wet or windy weather at the drop of a hat, with the wood fired clay oven situated alongside giving inspiration for food lovers to enjoy this ideal entertainment and relaxation zone year round. The calm and tranquillity bely the fact that one is a mere ten minutes on foot to all the amenities on Church Road. \n\nGreystones town is thriving, and the peaceful surrounds of Erskine Avenue are within easy walking distance to the seafront, Marina Village, and nearby historical Delgany village. It is a very special place for families to put down roots as the many local primary and secondary schools are highly regarded, and the town enjoys an enviable array of eateries, boutique shops, supermarkets, cafes, cosy pubs, library, golf course and much more. For those who commute further afield the N/M11/M50, DART and bus routes bring Dublin city, Rosslare harbour and surrounding areas within easy reach."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall / Front Porch - \nEntering the front of the house through a tiled, covered porch, into spacious entrance hall with understairs storage closet, ceiling rose and accessing:\n\nKitchen / Breakfast Room - 2.70m x 3.66m / 2.94m x 3.97m\nRecessed downlighting and solid wooden flooring in kitchen. Floor and eye level units, stainless steel sink and drainer, tiled splashback and south - west facing windows overlooking the rear garden. Integrated NordMende electric oven, grill, microwave, electric hob and extractor fan, NordMende dishwasher & provision for fridge/freezer. Stepping down to:\n\nReading Room / Den - 2.53m x 5.07m\nA bright room with window to the east facing front garden allowing morning light to stream in, while 3 skylights ensure natural light throughout the day. Built in wall shelving and ample power outlets. Leading to:\n\nUtility Room - 2.53m x 2.54m\nA fine size with ample space for storage, tiled floor, wall shelving, plumbed for washing machine and door to rear garden with outdoor gazebo located alongside.\n\nDining/ Living Room - 4.25m x 3.66m / 3.41m x 3.66m\nAn elegant, open plan room drenched in natural light owing to French doors and large windows overlooking the south westerly facing rear garden. Wood burning stove with wooden fireplace and granite hearth. Double doors leading to:\n\nSunroom - 6.30m x 2.59m\nA bright, south-west facing room with large windows and opening via French doors to an attractive paved terrace in the rear garden.\n\nOffice - 2.89m x 2.59m\nTiled floor and window overlooking the rear garden -an ideal space to work from home.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.59m x 5.40m\nA dual aspect, generously proportioned double bedroom with ample space for dressing or seating area. Off which:\n\n“Jack and Jill” Bathroom - 1.94m x 2.10m\nFully tiled floor and walls, frosted window, WC, pedestal wash hand basin with wall mounted mirror and vanity light above. Electric Mira shower with glazed surround. Also serving:\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.70m x 5.40m\nAn exceptionally large double bedroom with window to the private east facing front garden. Access to the floored attic via Stira staircase.\n\nTV Room / Bedroom 5 - 3.36m x 4.33m\nEntered from the entrance hall, a cosy room with wood burning stove, tiled fireplace and granite hearth. Built in storage and private outlook to greenery in front garden.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.20m x 1.75m\nOverlooking the front garden, a single bedroom with built in wardrobe and shelving.\n\nBathroom - 2.21m x 1.94m\nRecessed downlighting, frosted window, WC, pedestal wash hand basin, bath with tiled surround and shower attachment. Shelved hotpress access.\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nMain Bedroom Suite - 4.55m x 4.23m\nLarge double bedroom with eaves access for extensive storage. Bright dressing area with banks of built in wardrobes and window overlooking the colourful rear garden. Off which:\n\nEnsuite Shower Room - 2.44m x 2.25m\nRecessed downlighting, tiled walk-in shower with glazed surround, pedestal wash hand basin with wall mounted mirror and vanity light above, WC, skylight and access to eaves storage.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Generously appointed detached dormer bungalow in the heart of The Burnaby</li><li>Walking distance to all village amenities including seafront and DART</li><li>Potential for development of 0.75 acre site</li><li>Mature gardens boasting a stunning variety of mature flora, fauna and trees</li><li>Usual mains water with oil fired central heating and 2 wood burning stoves</ul>"
      },
